@node CMacs AI Providers
@section Providers

Eight providers are wired through the same @code{cmacs-ai-client-new}
DEFUN:

@table @code
@item claude
Anthropic Claude (HTTP).  Reads @env{ANTHROPIC_API_KEY} or
@env{CLAUDE_API_KEY}.
@item openai
OpenAI GPT (HTTP).  Reads @env{OPENAI_API_KEY}.
@item gemini
Google Gemini (HTTP).  Reads @env{GEMINI_API_KEY}.
@item grok
xAI Grok (HTTP).  Reads @env{XAI_API_KEY} or @env{GROK_API_KEY}.
@item ollama
Ollama (local HTTP).  Reads @env{OLLAMA_HOST}.
@item claude-code
The @command{claude} CLI in @option{--print} mode.
@item opencode
The @command{opencode} CLI.
@item claude-tmux
@command{claude} driven via an ephemeral tmux session.
@end table

@node CMacs AI Chat Buffers
@section Chat Buffers

@kbd{M-x cmacs-ai-chat} opens a fresh chat buffer in
@code{cmacs-ai-chat-mode} (derived from @code{org-mode}).  The
buffer layout mirrors @code{cmacs-libreclaw-room-mode}:

@example
#+TITLE: cmacs-ai -- 2026-05-25 18:00:00
#+PROPERTY: provider claude

* Conversation
** 18:00:00  user
What is GLib?
** 18:00:00  assistant
GLib is a low-level C utility library...
* Compose                                              :compose:
@end example

History above the @code{* Compose} sentinel is read-only; the
region below is the editable prompt area.  @kbd{C-c C-c} sends the
compose body and streams the response into a fresh @code{** assistant}
heading via the @code{AiStreamable} signal pipeline.

@table @kbd
@item C-c C-c
Send the compose region.
@item C-c C-k
Cancel an in-flight request.
@item C-c C-l
Clear conversation history (server-side and visible).
@item C-c C-s
Save the chat buffer to @code{cmacs-ai-chat-dir} (auto-saved on
every assistant turn as well).
@end table

@node CMacs AI Region Commands
@section Region Commands

Acting on the active region without opening a chat buffer:

@table @kbd
@item M-x cmacs-ai-rewrite-region
Prompt for an instruction; replace the region with the AI rewrite.
The current major mode is conveyed so the output uses the right
syntax.  Wrapped in one undo step.
@item M-x cmacs-ai-explain-region
Pop a side window with an Org-mode explanation of the region.
@item M-x cmacs-ai-doc-region
Insert an AI-written doc comment above the region (idiom matches
the language: docstring for Python/Elisp, @code{/** */} for
JavaDoc/Doxygen, etc.).
@item M-x cmacs-ai-test-region
Synthesize a unit test in a scratch buffer.
@end table

A right-click context menu entry is installed via
@code{cmacs-ai-context-menu-install}.

@node CMacs AI Inline Completion
@section Inline Ghost-Text Completion

@code{cmacs-ai-completion-mode} is a minor mode that drives idle-
timer-based fill-in-the-middle completion.  After
@code{cmacs-ai-completion-idle-delay} seconds of no input, a request
is fired with the buffer prefix + suffix as FIM context; the result
renders as a @code{shadow}-faced after-string overlay.  @kbd{TAB}
accepts; any other key dismisses.

Default provider is @code{claude-code} (CLI wrapper) so per-keystroke
HTTP costs are avoided; override with
@code{cmacs-ai-completion-provider}.

@node CMacs AI Voice Loop
@section Voice Loop

@kbd{M-x cmacs-ai-voice-chat} opens a chat buffer wired for full
voice round-trip: whisper transcribes a held-down recording via
@code{cmacs-whisper-dictate}, ai-glib streams the reply, and
@code{cmacs-piper-speak-region} speaks each completed sentence as
it streams in.  All four subsystems (@code{cmacs-whisper},
@code{cmacs-piper}, @code{cmacs-audio}, @code{cmacs-ai}) must be
enabled.

@table @code
@item cmacs-ai-voice-auto-speak
Whether replies are spoken.  Default @code{t}.
@end table

@node CMacs AI Coding Agent
@section Coding Agent

@kbd{M-x cmacs-ai-agent-open} opens (or resumes) the agent chat
for the current project root.  Before the first turn, it builds a
project-aware system prompt:

@itemize
@item
The first matching file from @code{cmacs-ai-agent-project-files}
(default: CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, README.org, README.md) is read in
full and attached as ``Project agent contract''.
@item
The absolute project root path is included.
@end itemize

This makes the assistant honor the project's own conventions
without manual cut-and-paste.

@node CMacs AI Tool Use
@section Tool Use

@code{cmacs-ai-tools-new} returns an @code{AiToolExecutor} handle
with all of ai-glib's built-ins pre-registered:

@itemize @bullet
@item @code{bash} -- run a shell command
@item @code{read} / @code{write} / @code{edit} -- file I/O
@item @code{glob} / @code{grep} / @code{ls} -- file discovery
@item @code{web_fetch} -- fetch a URL (capped at 100 KB)
@end itemize

Per the project default, all tools are enabled (full trust).
Set @code{cmacs-ai-tool-confirm} to @code{'destructive} for a
prompt before bash/write/edit, or to a function for per-call
custom approval.

Custom Elisp tools are registered via
@code{cmacs-ai-tools-register}; the callback is invoked with
@code{(NAME INPUT-JSON ID)} on each model call.

@node CMacs AI Image Generation
@section Image Generation

@code{cmacs-ai-image-generate-async} drives OpenAI / Gemini / Grok
image-generator interfaces and fires a callback with a plist of
@code{(:url U :base64 B :mime M :revised R)} entries.

@node CMacs AI Org Blocks
@section Org Babel Integration

@code{cmacs-ai-org-block-register} adds an @code{ai} language to
@code{org-babel-load-languages}:

@example
#+BEGIN_SRC ai :provider claude :system "Be brief"
Explain the GIL.
#+END_SRC
@end example

@kbd{C-c C-c} on the block sends the body and inserts the response
in @code{#+RESULTS:}.

@node CMacs AI GObject Introspection
@section GObject Introspection

The cmacs-ai init path prepends @code{$top_srcdir/deps/ai-glib/build/release}
to GIRepository's search path and eagerly requires @code{AiGlib-1.0}.
After @code{init_cmacs_ai} runs, the typelib is reachable from:

@itemize @bullet
@item Elisp: @code{(gi-require "AiGlib" "1.0")} returns @code{t}
without any manual @env{GI_TYPELIB_PATH} setup.
@item The bacon @code{cmacsgi} builtin: @code{cmacsgi eval "(gi-require
\"AiGlib\" \"1.0\")"}.
@item The MCP @code{gi_*} tools (@code{gi_list_namespaces},
@code{gi_describe}, @code{gi_call}).
@end itemize

This is the same machinery used for all other GI-exposed cmacs
libraries; no per-class binding code is needed.

@node CMacs AI MCP Tools
@section MCP Tools

Built with @option{--with-cmacs-mcp}, three tools are exposed on the
cmacs MCP socket:

@table @code
@item ai_prompt
One-shot synchronous prompt.  Args: @code{prompt} (required),
@code{provider}, @code{system}.
@item ai_list_providers
Enumerate provider symbols.
@item ai_open_chat
Open a chat buffer (optionally seeded with a first prompt).  Returns
the buffer name.
@end table

External agents (e.g. an outer Claude Code instance) can drive the
in-editor AI through these tools.

@node CMacs AI Configuration
@section Configuration

@table @code
@item cmacs-ai-default-provider
Default provider symbol.  Default @code{claude}.
@item cmacs-ai-default-model
Default model string, or @code{nil} for the provider default.
@item cmacs-ai-system-prompt
System prompt for new chat sessions.
@item cmacs-ai-max-tokens
Default max output tokens.  Default @code{4096}.
@item cmacs-ai-enabled-tools
Built-in tools advertised to the model.
@item cmacs-ai-tool-confirm
@code{nil} (never prompt) / @code{'destructive} / function.
@item cmacs-ai-chat-dir
Where auto-saved chats land.
@item cmacs-ai-config-file
Path to ai-glib's optional YAML config
(@file{~/.config/ai-glib/config.yaml} by default).  Honored by
ai-glib's @code{AiConfig} singleton; this defcustom is
informational only.
@end table

API keys are sourced from environment variables (see Providers
above) or from @file{~/.config/ai-glib/config.yaml}.
